===============================================================================

                                TuxFrw-NFT
                                ----------

            The ultimate Linux firewall automation tool using nftables.

===============================================================================

TuxFrw-NFT is a complete firewall automation tool for GNU/Linux based on nftables.

Currently, TuxFrw-NFT consists of modular script files created to simplify and
automate the way Linux nftables firewall rules are configured and applied.
With TuxFrw-NFT, an administrator can configure a complete Linux/Netfilter
firewall simply by providing IP addresses, network interfaces and policy definitions.

Features:
- Full nftables atomic ruleset compilation and execution (nft -f).
- Modular architecture (tf_BASE, tf_KERNEL, and per-direction rule modules).
- Stateful packet filtering (conntrack / ct state).
- Ingress raw packet filtering via netdev hook (BOGONs, spoofing, TCP flag attacks).
- Complete Dual-Stack support (IPv4 and IPv6).
- Traditional Gateway / DMZ / NAT mode (EXT, INT, DMZ, VPNs).
- Native Docker compatibility mode (DOCKER_SUPPORT="1"): protects the host on INPUT
  and controls container access on FORWARD (via tf_DOCKER.mod) without flushing or
  interfering with Docker container networking and DNAT.

Visit TuxFrw home page and get its latest version at:
 <https://tuxfrw.linuxinfo.com.br/>


Requirements
============

- Linux kernel with nftables support (nf_tables subsystem);
- nftables utility (nft) installed (version 0.9.x or higher);
- Bash shell.


Installation
============

Read the INSTALL file for installation instructions. Configuration and modules
are located in /etc/tuxfrw-nft and the executable is placed in /usr/sbin/tuxfrw-nft.


Usage
=====

# tuxfrw-nft {start|stop|load <module>|natopen|status|restart|panic}

Examples:
  tuxfrw-nft start
  tuxfrw-nft stop
  tuxfrw-nft status
  tuxfrw-nft load INPUT
  tuxfrw-nft load DOCKER
  tuxfrw-nft load INT-EXT


